## Honey Bee

I randomly started craving honey, which made me think about how amazing it is that bees can produce it, turning the essence of nectar gathered from all kinds of flowers into one. The next day, I felt like going for a morning run since it had been a while. Coincidentally, the nursery park had been expanded and planted with lots of sunflowers. The moment I ran past a flower with a few bees landing on it, I was instantly struck by how beautiful that process is, so I casually took some photos and videos.

When I got home, I posted a story about my awe for bees and the message in Surah An-Nahl (16:68–69). That night, after Isha prayer, I went to read the Quran, and MashaAllah, the exact page where I had left my last checkpoint was that very surah and those exact verses.

At this point im just holding back tears; it’s such a beautiful coincidence that felt like Allah was communicating with me. It just goes to show that many things fall into place by themselves, and we can only control so much in this dunya. Alhamdulillah for what we have, for what we don’t have, and for what we might have. May us pray for good blessings.

